"The model has no noise, and its lenses are ideal thin lenses, so the traced image distances agree with the thin lens equation to the {#} cm they are given to. Your own uncertainty is in where you put the object and the lenses. The demo calls the rays leaving an eyepiece parallel when their slopes agree to within {#}, which sets how well a microscope or telescope must be adjusted. Real lenses have thickness, spherical aberration and dispersion (color fringes), and a real eye’s near point varies from person to person.",
